      "conclusion": "Recovering the 382-row schema shift exposed that 66.58% of spend drove the highest CPA ($79.12), while click-led optimization trapped budget in low-converting older cohorts. Cutting $14,754 in zero-approved waste and reallocating toward 30-34 cohorts and Interest 29 can materially reduce CPA Approved."
