      "conclusion": "SLA speed alone protects regulatory compliance but does not lower consumer disputes. Substantive monetary and non-monetary relief cuts dispute rates by over half, making targeted front-line relief playbooks and sub-95% institutional SLA audits the highest-leverage path to reducing escalation."
